# Amos OS — init.rc additions for the no-UI Android base.
#
# Since the base Android has no Java UI framework / SystemUI, init must bring
# up our Rust stack headlessly. Order matters:
#   1) early-init: create the socket directory with correct owner/perms.
#   2) boot_completed: start the AI daemon (gRPC server over UDS).
#   3) The Tauri System UI is installed as the *only* launcher APK (HOME
#      category); Android auto-starts it as a system app once boot completes.
#
# Merge this file into the device's init.rc (e.g. device/<vendor>/<device>/
# init.rc or via TARGET_PROVIDES_INIT_RC) before building the OS image.

on early-init
    # Directory for the AI daemon's Unix Domain Socket + any shared state.
    mkdir /data/amos 0770 system system

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    # Bring up the AI inference daemon after core services are ready.
    # `setenv` + our CLI `--socket` flag ensure both daemon and Tauri agree on
    # the same UDS path even without the default.
    start amos-ai

# The AI daemon: a pure Rust binary shipped to /system/bin/amos-ai.
# - `oneshot` is NOT set: it is a long-running server and init restarts it if
#   it dies (default restart behavior for class main services).
# - `oom_score_adj` is lowered so the OS never kills the inference core.
service amos-ai /system/bin/amos-ai --socket /data/amos/ai.sock
    class main
    user root
    group root system
    seclabel u:r:system_app:s0
    setenv AMOS_SOCKET /data/amos/ai.sock
    oom_score_adj -1000

# Optional: restart policy — init restarts crashed services automatically for
# `class main`. To cap CPU/mem, wrap with a cgroup via:
#   write /dev/cpuset/top-app/cgroup.procs $PID   (in a companion service)
